nism to slow the pace of progress to a level that feels comfortable for legacy management structures.\n\nTo move forward, firms should shift investment from manual oversight layers to automated observability tooling. This reduces operational drag while increasing the auditability of every agentic transaction. By instrumenting the decision-making process itself, leaders can secure the benefits of speed without sacrificing the rigor required for regulatory compliance. This is not about removing humans from the process; it is about elevating them from bottlenecks to architects of the systems that define the next generation of enterprise performance.",
